  "gate": {
    "rule": "Pass only if all three hold on the randomised test set for the headline model, which is picked on dev as the candidate (s_linear, s_gbm, t_gbm, ct_gbm) with the highest area under the uplift curve (AUUC): (1) the 95% bootstrap interval on the incremental profit per customer of treating when predicted uplift exceeds cost over value has a lower bound above zero, so it beats treating nobody; (2) the 95% paired interval on that profit minus the profit of treating everyone has a lower bound above zero, so it beats blanket offers; (3) the 95% interval on the Qini coefficient has a lower bound above zero, so the ranking beats random targeting. Profit is estimated by inverse-probability weighting with the known randomisation. The cost and value are assumptions fixed before results.",
    "checks": {
      "beats_treating_nobody": true,
      "beats_treating_everybody": true,
